---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { BRAND_NAME } from "../lib/brand";
import {
  getBreadcrumbSchema,
  resolveSiteUrl,
} from "../lib/schemaMarkup";

const siteUrl = resolveSiteUrl(Astro.site);
const schema = [
  getBreadcrumbSchema(siteUrl, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Privacy", path: "/privacy" },
  ]),
];
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description={`${BRAND_NAME} privacy policy: what we store, who processes it, that we don't sell it, retention windows, export, and deletion.`}
  schema={schema}
>
  <article class="card max-w-3xl mx-auto my-8">
    <h1 class="card-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="card-subtitle">
      How ProbeHarbor handles your data (web and Android), who processes it, retention, and account deletion.
      Last updated October 9, 2026.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">What we store</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
      <li>Account email and auth metadata (Supabase Auth)</li>
      <li>Device and sensor configuration, temperature/humidity readings</li>
      <li>Alert settings and delivery audit logs</li>
      <li>Optional billing data via Stripe (we do not store card numbers)</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Freeze alerts</strong> (no account needed): your email, the place name you picked, and its location rounded to
        about 1&nbsp;km, used only to email you before freezing nights. Unsubscribing deletes the record.
      </li>
      <li>
        On the <strong>Android app</strong>: session tokens on-device; optional Firebase Cloud Messaging
        device tokens when you enable push (used only to deliver your alerts)
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">We don't sell your data</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      We don't sell or rent your personal information or sensor readings, and we don't share them for
      advertising. We use the services below only to run ProbeHarbor.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Services that process data for us</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong>: database, sign-in, and account emails</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: hosting, alert and notice email delivery, bot checks (Turnstile), and file storage for history archives and shared chart images</li>
      <li><strong>Stripe</strong>: billing, for paid plans</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> and <strong>Ahrefs</strong>: traffic analytics on marketing pages only (see <a class="text-link" href="#analytics">Analytics</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>Sentry</strong>: error reports so we can fix bugs</li>
      <li><strong>Firebase Cloud Messaging</strong>: push notifications, if you turn them on</li>
      <li><strong>OpenWeather</strong> and the <strong>National Weather Service</strong>: the city or ZIP you search and the location you pick, to look up places and forecasts</li>
      <li>
        Only if you set them up: the alert channels you choose (SMS through Twilio, Discord, Slack, Telegram,
        Microsoft Teams, ntfy, Pushover, WhatsApp, or your own webhook) receive the alert messages, and
        Google Nest or Ecobee when you connect a thermostat
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Android app</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      The ProbeHarbor Android app (`dev.probeharbor.android`; early-access builds use `dev.thermaltrace.android`) is a client for this website. It does
      <strong>not</strong> read temperature from the phone. It signs in with your ProbeHarbor account and
      loads the same household readings and settings over HTTPS. Push notifications are optional and can be
      turned off in the app (Account) and under Alert settings on the web.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Retention</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      Raw sensor readings roll up and expire on a schedule (90 days default on Free; longer on paid plans).
      You can set a custom retention window under Dashboard → Settings. Archived snapshots may be stored in
      cold storage for Pro households and are deleted along with the household.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Export & deletion</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      Export JSON anytime from <a class="text-link" href="/api/user/export">/api/user/export</a> while signed in.
      Delete your account under Dashboard → Settings. This removes your sign-in, alert settings, push device
      tokens, and shared chart images, plus any household you own alone, with its devices, readings, and
      cold-storage archives. In a shared household, ownership passes to another member and the household stays.
      Account deletion on the website also applies to Android app access.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm">
      What stays elsewhere: Stripe keeps its own billing records for paid plans, as the law requires, and our
      hosting providers may hold encrypted backups for a limited time under their own policies. We don't
      restore deleted accounts from them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Push notifications</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      Browser Web Push uses VAPID keys we control. The Android app may register an FCM device token when
      you enable push. Tokens are stored to deliver your household’s alerts and are removed when you
      disable push, sign out of push on that device, or delete your account. We do not sell push tokens.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2" id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
    <p class="text-sm mb-0">
      On public marketing pages (production), we load Google Analytics (GA4) and Ahrefs Web Analytics to
      understand traffic and referrals. Those scripts are not loaded on <code>/dashboard</code> or
      <code>/api</code> routes (except a few conversion thank-you paths). Product funnel events sent to GA
      are anonymized and never include live temperature readings. A short on-page notice appears the first
      time you visit a marketing page; dismissing it only hides the notice in this browser.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-sm mb-0">
      Privacy questions: <a class="text-link" href="/contact">Contact</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
